🚀 PIPELINE 1 — Coding APIs → Kafka → Snowflake
✅ Project Structure
api-kafka-snowflake/
│
├── producer.py
├── consumer.py
├── requirements.txt
├── .env.example
├── .gitignore
├── README.md

✅ STEP 1 — Initialize Git
git init

✅ STEP 2 — Create .gitignore
.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc

✅ STEP 3 — Create .env.example
SNOWFLAKE_USER=your_user
SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD=your_password
SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT=your_account
SNOWFLAKE_WAREHOUSE=COMPUTE_WH
SNOWFLAKE_DATABASE=ACADEMIC_INTELLIGENCE
SNOWFLAKE_SCHEMA=PUBLIC

KAFKA_SERVER=localhost:9092

✅ STEP 4 — Install Dependencies
pip install kafka-python snowflake-connector-python requests python-dotenv

✅ STEP 5 — Create requirements.txt
pip freeze > requirements.txt

✅ STEP 6 — Start Kafka Server
cd C:\kafka
bin\windows\kafka-server-start.bat config\server.properties

✅ STEP 7 — Create Kafka Topic
cd C:\kafka\bin\windows
kafka-topics.bat --create --topic apitopic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

✅ STEP 8 — Run Consumer
python api_consumer.py

✅ STEP 9 — Run Producer
python api_producer.py

✅ STEP 10 — Git Commit
git add .
git commit -m "Added API to Kafka to Snowflake pipeline"

✅ STEP 11 — Push to GitHub
git branch -M main
git remote add origin YOUR_REPOSITORY_URL
git push -u origin main
